    <div id="screen-school" style="display: none;"><h2>🏫 The Colorado Schoolhouse</h2><div class="schoolhouse-box"><h3>📅 Attendance Tracker (CO Law: 172 Days)</h3><div class="stat-row"><span><strong>Days Completed:</strong> <span id="att-days">0</span> / 172</span><div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" id="att-bar" style="width:0%"></div></div></div><div class="stat-row"><span><strong>Hours Logged:</strong> <span id="att-hours">0</span> hrs / 688 hrs</span><div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" id="att-hours-bar" style="width:0%"></div></div></div><div style="display:flex; gap:10px; margin-top:10px;"><button onclick="logDay()" class="success" style="width:auto; padding:8px 15px;">Log 4-Hour School Day</button><button onclick="logDay(1)" class="success" style="width:auto; padding:8px 15px; background:#555;">Log 1-Hour Day</button></div></div><div class="schoolhouse-box"><h3>📊 Academic Transcript (CO Required Subjects)</h3><p style="font-size:0.85em; color:#aaa;">Hours are logged based on quests completed (2 hrs each) plus any custom hours below.</p><div id="transcript-list"></div><h4 style="margin-top:20px;">Log Custom Academic Hours</h4><div class="custom-hours-form"><select id="custom-subj"><option>Reading</option><option>Writing</option><option>Math</option><option>Science</option><option>History</option><option>Geography</option><option>Constitution</option><option>Economics</option><option>PE</option><option>Health</option><option>Art</option></select><input type="number" id="custom-hrs" placeholder="Hrs" min="1" max="8" style="width:60px;"><button onclick="addCustomHours()" style="width:auto; padding:8px 15px;">Add Hours</button></div></div></div>
    
    <div id="screen-library" style="display: none;"><h2>📚 The Village Library</h2><div class="library-box"><p style="text-align:center; font-size:0.85em; color:#aaa;">A curated knowledge graph of free, public domain, and government resources for holistic homeschooling.</p><div class="lib-category"><h4>🍂 Educational Philosophy & Nature Connection</h4><a href="https://rsarchive.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Rudolf Steiner Archive:</strong> Hundreds of lectures on Waldorf education and human development.</a><a href="https://waldorflibrary.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Waldorf Library:</strong> Curriculum ideas, festivals, and classroom resources.</a><a href="https://ourspirit.com" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Our Spirit (Douglas Gabriel):</strong> The Spirit of Childhood and seasonal lessons.</a></div><div class="lib-category"><h4>🧘 Taoist Internal Vitality & Self-Healing</h4><div class="lib-link" style="cursor: default;"><strong>The Eight Pillars of Taoism:</strong> Philosophy, Revitalization, Balanced Diet, Forgotten Food Diet, Healing Art, Sex Wisdom, Mastery, and Success.</div><div class="lib-link" style="cursor: default;"><strong>The Human Battery Model:</strong> Understanding the three-part bio-electric battery (Structure, Liquid, Electrical Charge/Chi).</div><div class="lib-link" style="cursor: default;"><strong>The Seven Glands (Wheel of Life):</strong> Sexual, Adrenal, Pancreas, Thymus, Thyroid, Pituitary, and Pineal glands.</div><div class="lib-link" style="cursor: default;"><strong>The Twelve Nerve Exercises:</strong> Dharma's methodology to soften and expand the nervous system for anti-aging and mental clarity.</div></div><div class="lib-category"><h4>🏔️ Colorado & Regional Learning</h4><a href="https://cpw.state.co.us" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Colorado Parks & Wildlife:</strong> Wildlife, ecology, fishing, geology, and conservation.</a><a href="https://extension.colostate.edu" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>CSU Extension:</strong> Free curriculum on gardening, soil, water, food preservation, and 4-H.</a><a href="https://conps.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Colorado Native Plant Society:</strong> Local botany and plant identification.</a></div><div class="lib-category"><h4>🔬 STEM & General Curriculum</h4><a href="https://www.coreknowledge.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Core Knowledge Foundation:</strong> Free, complete K-8 curriculum.</a><a href="https://www.ck12.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>CK-12:</strong> Free digital textbooks for math and science.</a><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/stem" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>NASA STEM:</strong> Space science and engineering resources.</a></div><div class="lib-category"><h4>🛡️ Preparedness, Health & Survival</h4><a href="https://www.ready.gov" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>FEMA / Ready.gov:</strong> Emergency plans, family preparedness, and natural disasters.</a><a href="https://hesperian.org" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>Hesperian Foundation:</strong> Free books like "Where There Is No Doctor" and "A Book for Midwives".</a><a href="https://www.nccih.nih.gov" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>NIH (NCCIH):</strong> Modern complementary and integrative health information.</a><a href="https://plants.usda.gov" target="_blank" class="lib-link"><strong>USDA Plants Database:</strong> Plant identification and taxonomy.</a></div></div></div>
    
    <div id="screen-commons" style="display: none;"><h2>🌍 The Village Commons</h2><div class="commons-box"><h3>Bridge to Permies</h3><p>Post your evidence to the <a href="https://permies.com/f/178/" target="_blank" style="color:#8bc34a;">PEP Forum</a> to get certified.</p></div><div class="commons-box"><h3>📦 Optional Add-on: The Offline Archive</h3><p>For families wanting to build a complete, offline civilizational backup drive, download these open-source files to a local hard drive.</p><div class="archive-list" style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #333; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 10px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.85em; color: #8bc34a; "><strong>[Medicine]</strong> Medical Library (67MB), Military Medicine (78MB)<br><strong>[Agriculture]</strong> FOSS Cooking (24MB), Gardening Q&A (923MB)<br><strong>[DIY]</strong> Woodworking Q&A (99MB), iFixit Guides (3380MB)<br><strong>[Maps]</strong> Download your state's .pmtiles from Project Nomad Maps repo.</div></div></div>
